# PIT Optimizer V5 final whole-branch fix-wave report

Date: 2026-09-05
Status: all Critical and Important findings 1-9 and minors 10-13 implemented and locally verified.
Base: `5a56874cc762831ab6997f4d550fa12f5c43d3cc`
Head: `3548febcb2c51cf5ed13c2dae6eadddeaa6ed5c8`
Commit: `fix(pit-optimizer-v5): close final execution and recovery gaps`
Scope: one coordinated wave, one local commit, 16 files, 1,265 insertions and 343 deletions.

The full design, learning-search plan, progress ledger, authoritative final-review findings, and
Task 9 report were read before implementation. The recorded rulings are preserved: all
close-derived scale-outs execute at the next eligible open; raw codecs are selected only by exact
typed authority edges; finite USD caps require authenticated model-price upper bounds and
prospective reservation; no ceiling remains unlimited. No subagents were spawned.

## Finding closure and implementation

1. **Typed raw campaign edges.** The real repository authenticates exact raw bytes only for the
   strictly decoded campaign manifest's panel-plan bundle/provenance edges. Raw authentication
   streams SHA-256 without JSON parsing, normalization, reference extraction, or the generic
   128 MiB JSON limit. Regular-file, containment, single-link, and before/open/after identity
   checks remain enforced. An artifact previously authenticated through a raw edge cannot acquire
   generic-JSON codec privilege through an alias. Existing explicit newline provenance handling
   remains intact. Windows raw identity compares supported stable identity/size/mtime attributes;
   POSIX retains the additional ctime comparison.

2. **Causal scale-out timing.** Completed-close exit decisions enqueue authenticated pending
   actions. Both close and scale-out actions execute at the next eligible open, using original
   position quantity for scale-out fractions. Invalid/missing opens leave the pending decision
   intact. Checkpoint serialization, symbol-transition remapping, tier state, and full-close
   removal remain coherent. Earlier same-bar target prices no longer receive hindsight fills.

3. **Wire-safe role messages.** The authenticated frozen internal request is unchanged. Only at
   the provider boundary, content is converted to canonical JSON text within plain role/content
   dictionaries. The wire envelope introduces no extra request fields.

4. **Durable scheduling cursor.** Terminal no-novel authority now carries full before/after
   scheduling cursors, archive identity, attempted novelty keys, and an authenticated outcome
   chain. Production recovery reconstructs checkpoint-owned finalized records and actual terminal
   investigator packages chronologically, keeping archive promotion checkpoint-only. Runtime
   independently recomputes selected-parent novelty, cursor advance, state digests, and complete
   reconstructible parent-pool exhaustion. Round N+1 advances; completed/terminal N can be resumed
   after later progress without repeating paid work or changing the archive.

5. **Lineage-aware investigator memory.** The arbitrary last-12 slice is replaced by the actual
   selected-parent lineage projector under authenticated `investigator_memory_max_bytes`
   (default 96 KiB). Mandatory lineage evidence is preserved. Authenticated prior critic packages
   supply original comparative assessment, next campaign direction, causal reviews, and real
   reissued evidence citations. Full-feedback entries retain hypotheses, predictions,
   implementation instructions, provenance, and supporting evidence; summary entries remain
   bounded without discarding non-review outcomes.

6. **Causal critic evidence and usable author contracts.** Critic envelopes include bounded
   symbol-neutral activity, exposure, cash, friction, expectancy, excursion, exit/entry/intent and
   regime diagnostics, parent deltas, and up to eight actual bounded semantic-decision
   differences. The supported evidence/request budgets are explicit. Author contracts regenerate
   the trusted nested V3 snapshot/decision types, method surfaces, reason enums, ranking,
   allocation/capacity, exit/tier, add-on and AST/import/export invariants from real V3 contracts.
   These interface details participate in authenticated request identity.

7. **Prospective token/USD authority.** Provider capabilities authenticate per-model input/output
   price upper bounds and input framing overhead. Before a durable reservation or dispatch,
   the real ledger recomputes a conservative wire/schema input bound plus maximum output tokens,
   and reserves the corresponding worst-case USD where a finite ceiling exists. Finite ceilings
   without model-price authority fail closed; `None` does not restrict spend. Settlements and
   recovered reservations verify their bounds. Unknown transport outcomes consume their full
   reserved tokens and cost; over-bound receipts become accounting failures. Decimal prices,
   canonical identity and cumulative USD remain exact under low ambient Decimal precision.
   Retry and repair defaults remain zero.

8. **Truthful summary state.** Summary independently authenticates terminal round-outcome kinds
   and cleanup evidence. A runtime-failed campaign remains failed even when cleanup succeeds;
   cleanup success remains separately visible.

9. **Live deadline.** The authenticated minimum remaining role/round deadline reaches the
   one-shot provider. The concrete gateway uses the manifest role timeout, not an implicit
   30-second timeout. A single asynchronous SDK call is bounded by wall-clock cancellation,
   with zero retries and owned-client cleanup, and expires before reservation if no time remains.
   Only the V5 gateway method changed; existing V2-V4 gateway paths are untouched.

10. **Baseline champion fallback.** Reported best performance uses the authenticated baseline and
    common campaign contract with the normal champion selector, so an all-regressing archive
    cannot become the reported champion.

11. **Sibling behavioral deduplication.** Semantic-equivalent siblings receive the typed
    `sibling_equivalent` outcome and retain semantic metadata. Only the first behaviorally
    distinct representative reaches expensive quick/discovery evaluation. Deterministic resume
    reconstructs the same seen-fingerprint decisions.

12. **Escape permission versus activation.** Hypotheses explicitly choose authoring mode, with
    normal symbol edits as the default. Ordinary edits send only intended policy scope;
    cross-policy requests include their necessary policies. Manifest full-source permission no
    longer activates the escape automatically.

13. **Usable structural escape.** Explicitly authorized full-source edits can introduce declared
    validator-permitted private helper functions and uppercase constants. Undeclared top-level
    AST edits, import changes, and API-export changes remain rejected; normal symbol editing and
    closed validation remain intact.

Two adjacent integration defects exposed by direct execution were corrected rather than hidden:
the evaluator's typed report grid now matches quick-base-only plus four three-scenario discovery
episodes, and canonical typed authority encoding supports strict UTF-8 semantic-decision bytes.
Binary PIT artifacts still use only their explicit raw codec.

## Documentation and preserved boundaries

The plan's stale missing-critic paragraph now preserves authenticated precritic evidence with a
typed critic-unavailable result, no finalized experiment record, and no archive/checkpoint
promotion. Plan/spec text now documents prospective price/token reservation, explicit memory
budget, canonical transport, live deadlines, scheduling state separation, richer evidence,
structural-mode activation, typed raw edges, and next-open close-derived exits.

Provider-neutral domain/runtime separation, O'Neil core policies, annualized portfolio CAGR as
the primary objective, checkpoint-only archive promotion, V2-V4 readers/dispatch, confidentiality,
zero retry/repair defaults, and exact workspace crash-recovery code were preserved. The
pre-existing campaign-stage fail-closed `import-v4-candidate` deferral remains acknowledged.

## Deterministic direct-check evidence

The temporary direct fixture was run with:

```text
python -B .artifacts/v5_final_wave_smoke.py
ALL_DIRECT_CHECKS 28
```

The final run occurred after the independent runtime scheduling-proof validation was added. It
exercised real production composition, repository typed codecs and provider accounting with
bounded in-memory collaborators; it created no provider, Docker, Git-materialized candidate,
market-data, or replay workload. Its exact passing check labels were:

1. narrow normal author scope, explicit structural opt-in, complete nested V3 contracts
2. provider messages encode frozen payload as canonical JSON text in plain dictionaries
3. full-source structural helper and constant additions render while preserving imports and exports
4. full-source undeclared import edits rejected
5. raw exact-byte digest mismatch rejected
6. manifest plan raw edges authenticate non-JSON bytes without JSON decoding
7. generic alias to authorized raw artifact remains fail-closed
8. finite USD budget without authenticated model prices rejected
9. prospective input plus output token and authenticated model-price reservation; no-cap unrestricted
10. full deterministic investigator-author-critic round, sibling semantic dedup, one quick and four episodes, checkpoint promotion
11. critic receives quick-base plus full discovery grid, parent deltas, causal diagnostics, and actual semantic traces
12. completed round resumes idempotently without role, candidate, or publication work
13. operator champion remains baseline when every candidate regresses
14. next investigator receives authenticated campaign direction and lineage-budgeted prior experiment evidence
15. two-parent no-novel cursor advances N+1, exhausts only complete pool, preserves checkpoint, and resumes N/N+1 idempotently
16. full scheduling cursor and exhaustion history authenticate through durable typed round codecs
17. insufficient prospective input plus maximum output tokens reject before reservation and dispatch
18. insufficient prospective USD rejects before reservation and dispatch
19. authenticated reservation settles exact reported usage and recovers without spending again
20. unknown transport outcome consumes its full reserved tokens and cost with zero retry
21. receipt exceeding authenticated cost upper bound becomes accounting failure
22. no USD ceiling permits reported spend above finite-cap examples
23. one-shot gateway uses canonical wire messages and authenticated remaining timeout above fixed 30 seconds
24. live provider coroutine cancels at wall deadline
25. close-derived scale-out queues without historical fill, survives missing open/checkpoint/remap, and fills next eligible open
26. runtime failure remains failed in later summary despite successful cleanup
27. price authority hashing and cumulative USD remain exact under low ambient Decimal precision
28. streamed raw codec authenticates synthetic 129 MiB input without generic JSON-size cap

Important fixture observations:

- Three byte-distinct variants with equal behavior produced one quick evaluation, four discovery
  episodes, two sibling-equivalent records, exactly three fixture role calls, and one checkpoint
  promotion. Completed-round recovery performed no extra calls, candidates, or publications.
  The regressing evaluated candidate did not replace the authenticated baseline champion.
- A capacity-two archive with three completed rounds was followed by round-four no-novel and
  round-five exhausted outcomes. Both parents were covered, checkpoint generation stayed at
  three, and round-four/round-five resumes remained idempotent before and after later progress.
- The actual local authorization ledger serialized and recovered typed reservations and
  receipts. Insufficient prospective token/USD limits prevented both reservation and dispatch;
  accepted fake usage settled at 50 tokens and USD 0.001; unknown usage consumed the exact
  reservation; uncapped usage accepted USD 50.
- The one-shot transport used a synthetic hosted-client coroutine with a granted 120-second
  timeout (not 30), and a separate 30-millisecond deadline canceled the coroutine. No SDK
  network request was sent.
- Actual simulator methods observed synthetic high 130/close 99, did not create a historical
  120 fill, survived a missing next open and AAA-to-BBB remap, then filled 2.5 shares at the
  next eligible open of 97. Pending-intent checkpoint round-trip was exercised.
- Raw authentication used the temporary fixture's own exact source bytes for the local
  Windows file check. The 129 MiB case was a bounded simulated stream reusing a 1 MiB block,
  not a real PIT artifact or a large on-disk temporary file.

## Compile, import, lint, isolation, and commit checks

Fresh after-commit direct compilation and imports reported:

```text
PASS compile 29 source files; import 33 modules; installed async SDK surface
PASS provider-neutral domain/runtime import coupling
PASS legacy gateway/simulator AST unchanged outside three V5 methods and pending V5 intent validation
PASS no test files, O'Neil core policy changes, or V2-V4 dispatch edits; temporary fixture removed
```

Compilation used the built-in `compile` on all 27 V5 source files plus `agent_loop.py` and
`core/backtest_engine.py`, with `python -B -` and no bytecode output. Imports covered 26 V5
modules plus the backtest, gateway, legacy command/controller/artifacts/evaluation/authorization
modules. Installed `AsyncCompletions.create` was checked via `inspect.unwrap` without calling it.

The AST comparison against the base commit proved all legacy gateway/simulator AST unchanged
except `OpenRouterGateway.request_pit_optimizer_v5_json_once`,
`PortfolioSimulator._execute_v5_pending_policy_exits`,
`PortfolioSimulator._check_exits_v5_after_close`, and
`PendingPolicyExit.__post_init__`. Import AST checks covered search, selection, memory,
runtime, contracts, and provider against legacy controller/concrete provider coupling.

Commands passed before and after commit:

```text
python -B -m ruff check core/pit_optimizer_v5 agent_loop.py core/backtest_engine.py
All checks passed!
python -B -m ruff format --check <the 12 changed V5 Python files>
12 files already formatted
git diff --check
git diff --cached --check
git diff HEAD^ HEAD --check
git status --porcelain=v1
```

The final status command returned no entries. Local commit hooks passed Ruff, trailing whitespace,
end-of-file, and merge-conflict checks; YAML had no applicable files. Shared Git metadata required
the authorized sandbox escalation; staging and commit then succeeded. No hook requested network
installation. The temporary fixture was deleted with an exact-path patch before staging, and
`Test-Path .artifacts/v5_final_wave_smoke.py` returned `False`. Reports remain in the existing
ignored SDD evidence directory, outside the source commit.

## Remaining concerns and handoff

- No live provider, Docker/image/container, Git materialization, PIT market data, network,
  replay, test file/suite, push, or merge operation was performed. Empirical optimizer returns
  and live-service behavior are therefore not claimed as validated by this wave.
- Finite-cost configurations need the new authenticated per-model price upper bounds. Existing
  prototype V5 manifests/cursors/authorities that lack newly required typed fields need
  regeneration/re-authentication before reuse; they are not silently repaired. No-ceiling
  campaigns remain unlimited.
- The previously acknowledged fail-closed campaign-stage `import-v4-candidate` deferral remains.
- No known unclosed final-review finding remains. The branch/worktree is preserved, committed,
  and ready for the controller's independent final disposition.
